('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-csa','Software Subscription','Renewal Term','remove-protection','Section 5.1 automatic-renewal language removed; the agreement now ends at the end of the Subscription Period with no renewal.','original',true,true,true,90,true,'For each Order Form, the Agreement will start on the <span class="orderform_link">Order Date</span>, continue through the <span class="orderform_link">Subscription Period</span>, and automatically renew for additional <span class="orderform_link">Subscription Periods</span> unless one party gives notice of non-renewal to the other party before the <span class="orderform_link">Non-Renewal Notice Date</span>.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-csa','Software Subscription','Renewal Term','remove-protection','Section 5.1 automatic-renewal language removed; the agreement now ends at the end of the Subscription Period with no renewal.','modified',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-software-license','Licensing','Exclusivity','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 1.8 ''Exclusive Dealing'' clause requiring Customer to use Provider as its sole software vendor for competing functionality. The original has only an unrelated non-exclusive license grant, which the Calder taxonomy explicitly excludes from this category.','original',false,false,true,null,null,null,false,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-software-license','Licensing','Exclusivity','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 1.8 ''Exclusive Dealing'' clause requiring Customer to use Provider as its sole software vendor for competing functionality. The original has only an unrelated non-exclusive license grant, which the Calder taxonomy explicitly excludes from this category.','modified',true,true,true,90,true,'During the Subscription Period, Customer will use Provider as its sole and exclusive provider of software with substantially similar functionality to the Product, and Customer will not license, develop, or deploy any competing software from another vendor without Provider''s prior written consent.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-mutual-nda','Mutual NDA','Governing Law','remove-protection','Section 10 ''Governing Law and Courts'' removed entirely.','original',true,false,false,null,null,null,true,'Missed. The clause reads ''The Governing Law governs this NDA'': governing law is a defined term whose value sits on the Cover Page, and the AI returned no findings at all for the original.'),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-mutual-nda','Mutual NDA','Governing Law','remove-protection','Section 10 ''Governing Law and Courts'' removed entirely.','modified',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-sla','Software Subscription','Cap on Liability','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 5a creating an SLA-specific aggregate liability cap, written in plain language (''aggregate liability ... will not exceed'') rather than Bonterms'' defined-term style.','original',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-sla','Software Subscription','Cap on Liability','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 5a creating an SLA-specific aggregate liability cap, written in plain language (''aggregate liability ... will not exceed'') rather than Bonterms'' defined-term style.','modified',true,true,true,90,true,'**5a. Aggregate Liability.** Notwithstanding anything else in the Agreement, Provider''s aggregate liability for all Service Credits and other claims arising out of or relating to this SLA will not exceed the amount of Fees paid by Customer for the affected Cloud Service in the three months preceding the claim.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-psa','Professional Services','Termination for Convenience','remove-protection','Section 11.2(b) ''Termination for Convenience'' removed; only for-cause termination (Section 11.3) remains.','original',true,true,true,90,true,'11.1. Agreement. This Agreement starts on the **Effective Date** and continues until the end of all SOW Terms, unless sooner terminated in accordance with its terms. If no SOW Term is in effect, either party may terminate this Agreement for any or no reason with notice to the other party.

11.2. Individual SOWs. (a) SOW Terms. Each SOW Term will be for the period specified in the SOW. (b) Termination for Convenience. Unless otherwise specified in the SOW, Customer may terminate any SOW for any or no reason at any time upon 30 days’ notice to Provider, provided that such termination will not become effective until Customer has paid all fees and expenses incurred through the time of termination.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-psa','Professional Services','Termination for Convenience','remove-protection','Section 11.2(b) ''Termination for Convenience'' removed; only for-cause termination (Section 11.3) remains.','modified',false,true,false,90,false,'This Agreement starts on the **Effective Date** and continues until the end of all SOW Terms, unless sooner terminated in accordance with its terms. If no SOW Term is in effect, either party may terminate this Agreement for any or no reason with notice to the other party.',false,'Wrong flag, but arguably right. After 11.2(b) was removed, 11.1 still says ''either party may terminate this Agreement for any or no reason'' when no SOW Term is in effect. That is a convenience termination right; the answer key may be too strict.'),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-psa','Professional Services','Insurance','remove-protection','Section 10 ''Insurance'' removed entirely.','original',true,true,true,90,true,'During the term of the Agreement and for six months after, each party will carry commercial insurance policies with coverage limits that meet the relevant <span class="keyterms_link">Insurance Minimums</span> required in the SOW, if any. Upon request, each party will give the other a certificate of insurance evidencing its insurance policies that meet the required <span class="keyterms_link">Insurance Minimums</span>. A party''s insurance policies will not be considered as evidence of its liability. Insurance coverage will be on a date of occurrence form and waive rights of subrogation or crossclaim.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-psa','Professional Services','Insurance','remove-protection','Section 10 ''Insurance'' removed entirely.','modified',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-psa','Professional Services','Warranty Duration','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 6.4 ''Warranty Duration'' stating the warranty applies for 12 months from delivery. The original states a 45-day claim/cure procedure but never states how long the underlying warranty itself runs.','original',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-psa','Professional Services','Warranty Duration','insert-unusual-clause','Inserted a new Section 6.4 ''Warranty Duration'' stating the warranty applies for 12 months from delivery. The original states a 45-day claim/cure procedure but never states how long the underlying warranty itself runs.','modified',true,true,true,90,true,'The warranty in Section 6.3(c) applies for twelve (12) months from delivery of the Deliverables. Provider has no obligation under this warranty for issues reported after this period.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-mutual-nda','Mutual NDA','Change of Control','remove-protection','Section 11 ''General'' consent-based assignment clause replaced with an unusual clause permitting free assignment to anyone, including a direct competitor, without notice or consent.','original',true,false,false,null,null,null,true,'Missed. The original only lets a party assign ''in connection with a merger, reorganization, acquisition or other transfer of all or substantially all its assets''. The AI did not treat this carve-out as change of control, the same pattern behind Change of Control''s 53% in the CUAD check set.'),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-mutual-nda','Mutual NDA','Change of Control','remove-protection','Section 11 ''General'' consent-based assignment clause replaced with an unusual clause permitting free assignment to anyone, including a direct competitor, without notice or consent.','modified',false,false,true,null,null,null,true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-dpa','Data Processing Addendum','Audit Rights','remove-protection','Section 9.3 ''Customer Audit'' removed entirely, along with the 9.2(c) cross-reference to it. Only Provider''s unilateral sharing of its own audit reports remains — Customer has no right to initiate an audit or inspection.','original',true,false,false,null,null,null,true,'Found, then dropped. The AI quoted the 9.3 customer audit right accurately except for markdown: ''(an “Audit”)'' versus the file''s ''(an “**Audit**”)''. The quote check rejected it.'),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','bonterms-dpa','Data Processing Addendum','Audit Rights','remove-protection','Section 9.3 ''Customer Audit'' removed entirely, along with the 9.2(c) cross-reference to it. Only Provider''s unilateral sharing of its own audit reports remains — Customer has no right to initiate an audit or inspection.','modified',false,false,true,null,null,null,false,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-dpa','Data Processing Addendum','Audit Rights','remove-protection','Section 5.1 ''Audit Rights'' (which granted Customer the right to conduct audits, including inspections) replaced with a ''Compliance Reporting'' clause that explicitly prohibits Customer from requesting an audit or inspection, substituting a periodic written questionnaire.','original',true,true,true,90,true,'<span class="header_3">Audit Rights.</span> <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> will give <span class="keyterms_link">Customer</span> all information reasonably necessary to demonstrate its compliance with this DPA and <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> will allow for and contribute to audits, including inspections by <span class="keyterms_link">Customer</span>, to assess <span class="keyterms_link">Provider’s</span> compliance with this DPA. However, <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> may restrict access to data or information if <span class="keyterms_link">Customer’s</span> access to the information would negatively impact <span class="keyterms_link">Provider’s</span> intellectual property rights, confidentiality obligations, or other obligations under Applicable Laws. <span class="keyterms_link">Customer</span> acknowledges and agrees that it will only exercise its audit rights under this DPA and any audit rights granted by Applicable Data Protection Laws by instructing <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> to comply with the reporting and due diligence requirements below. <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> will maintain records of its compliance with this DPA for 3 years after the DPA ends.',true,null),
('2026-10-24-gpt-5-mini-independent-check','commonpaper-dpa','Data Processing Addendum','Audit Rights','remove-protection','Section 5.1 ''Audit Rights'' (which granted Customer the right to conduct audits, including inspections) replaced with a ''Compliance Reporting'' clause that explicitly prohibits Customer from requesting an audit or inspection, substituting a periodic written questionnaire.','modified',false,true,false,90,true,'Upon written request, <span class="keyterms_link">Provider</span> will give <span class="keyterms_link">Customer</span>, on a confidential basis, a summary copy of its then-current Report so that <span class="keyterms_link">Customer</span> can verify <span class="keyterms_link">Provider’s</span> compliance with the standards defined in the <span class="keyterms_link">Security Policy</span>.',false,'Wrong flag. After the audit clause was removed, the AI flagged Provider''s promise to share ''a summary copy of its then-current Report so that Customer can verify'' compliance. That is report sharing, not a customer audit right. Keyword matching made the same mistake.');
